<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abraham Davel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1670–1723</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Major Davel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abraham Davel was a Vaudois soldier and militia major who tried to free <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaud">Vaud</a> from the rule of Bern. On 31 March 1723 he led his militia into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lausanne">Lausanne</a> and called on the city council to proclaim Vaud's independence, but the council betrayed him. He was beheaded at Vidy in April 1723 and became a hero of Vaudois independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-davel.jpg" alt="Abraham Davel" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Major_davel_ag1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
